  "steps": [
    "Heat the milk in a vessel and once it is warm (dip a finger in it and it shouldn’t be too hot), add vinegar/ lemon juice to it slowly while stirring.",
    "Wait for 2-3 mins and once the whey water has separated, strain it in a muslin cloth and keep this aside to set.",
    "In a non-stick pan, add olive oil and saute onions on low heat until golden brown and caramelised.",
    "In a Blender, add paneer and greek yogurt and blend until it is creamy. Yoy may add more curd if needed to make it lighter.",
    "Now add the seasonings, caramelised onions and freshly chopped basil to this creamt base.",
    "Spread it on toasted sesame bagels and enjoy."
  ],
  "assumptions": [
    "The 1.5 litres of milk makes about 150 g low-fat paneer. The creator uses Pride of Cows fat-free milk (10 litres for Rs 999)."
